{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cities, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation, and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights, delicious street food (ramen, takoyaki – I tried it all!), and the organized chaos of Shibuya Crossing were unforgettable.  I spent hours exploring quirky shops in Harajuku and finding peace in the Meiji Jingu Shrine.\n\nNext, a bullet train whisked me away to Kyoto.  Here, the pace slowed considerably.  I wandered through the iconic Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates, and found tranquility in the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.  A traditional tea ceremony was a highlight – a beautiful and meditative experience.\n\nThe food was consistently incredible. From fresh sushi to delicate wagashi (Japanese sweets), every meal was a treat.  I even braved a conveyor belt sushi restaurant – a surprisingly fun experience!\n\nNavigating the language barrier was sometimes challenging, but the kindness and helpfulness of the Japanese people made it easy. I learned a few basic phrases, and even with limited communication, smiles and gestures went a long way.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions seamlessly blended with modern innovation.  It’s a place that captivates the senses and nourishes the soul.  I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968507617712021}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.10784334689378738}, {"token": "\n\n", 